 "floorplan_note": "cl2h: W-column SRAMs MY (rd_out/r_addr/clk pins on LEF x=0 now face the centre column). cl2dh CLOSED TT +97.07/FF +7.59 but native FAIL: launch 262.9 (75 rwq pins), capture 222.1 (612 c_d pins), boundary spread 95.3 around R 353.2 (one CTS root from the N clock pin: N c_d pin flops early, S rwq pin flops late; cl2e balanced-CTS gate spread 119.7, no gain). bfqf = same edges, face-local CTS roots clk_n (c_d pin regs) / clk_s (rwq pin regs) / clk core + 8 direct SRAM clock entries clk_m0..7 (VM q0 faces recipe, native PASS L193.2/C186.1). | cl2c (native audit of CLOSED cl2b TT +79.64/FF +12.38/DRC 0: capture rst_n 416.8 ps, mlo 200.2, mhi 194.3; R 343.8, spread 88.3): rst_n into a local reset relay at its pin; write-mask pair = one pin register each (was 8 per-macro copies ~250 um from the W pins); same edges. | cl2a GRT-0116 (547 overflow, 372 on M4) sat in the 20-um channel between the two macro columns (x 140-167): both columns face it with their W/E M4 pin rows (412 + 411 pins per array). cl2b: 64.8-um centre channel and ~45-um outer channels, 26-um row channels; the mask registers were already per macro (64 kept FFs), not the cause. | cl2d: c_d pin flops anchored at the N face (one register per pin); gate CTS spread 117.5 ps with the W-mid clock entry 149 um off the centre channel where the cq/OR/rwq sinks sit -> clock entry moved to the N face at the centre channel (x 151.1); outline 345.6 -> 302.4 wide (W/E empty margins 45.4 -> ~21.6 um core gap >= 20, the 65-um centre channel kept for cl2a's GRT lesson), fill 32 -> 36 %.",
